[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_2v8or")
item_name = "Arvid's Note 2"
item_type = 1
note_text = "\"To whoever they sent to replace me—because I know they already have.

I couldn't leave a digital trail on the network, and I knew that nobody from corporate would ever bother to crawl into this miserable old tunnel. They only care about data arrays; they don’t like getting their boots muddy.

Listen to me carefully: the administration is lying to us. This isn't a routine ecological survey of the Muscardinus population. The company knows exactly what is mutating the wildlife out here. They didn't send us to study an anomaly; they sent us to act as bait to map its behavior.

There is something out here in the black. It isn't an animal. It mimics, it watches, it stalks, and it wants to tear me apart. It’s been using the nests to track the literal frequency of my footsteps around the cabin.

But I am not going out quietly. I’ve managed to rig a trap for it. I bypassed the terminal’s main firewall and routed a localized high-frequency override through the cabin's primary anchor grid. If it triggers, it should sever whatever tether keeps that monster hunting in these coordinates.

I couldn't activate it from here before my battery died, but you can do it from the terminal in the house. You have to use my corporate override to bypass LUND's restrictions.

USER: STENBERG
PASSKEY: 1996

Go to the terminal, log me in, and execute the anchor protocol. Please. Don't let them win.

If you make it out of these woods alive, find a way to contact my family. Tell Linnea and Maja that their pappa misses them so much, and that I think of them every single single hour of the day, especially when the dark gets too heavy. I just want to come ho—

[The text ends completely abruptly, the pen dragging violently off the bottom edge of the paper in a sharp, jagged streak, leaving the word \"home\" unfinished.]\""
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://baixx1fs8cosb"
